# Copy to .env.local (gitignored). You almost certainly do not need to.
#
# With NOTHING set, the app is fully functional: every run key plays from a bundled
# JSONL recording in lib/donald/events.*.jsonl. That is how usedonald.com runs in
# production, and it is the supported path for local development.

# Point this at a REST API you self-host to make run keys outside RECORDED_RUNS stream
# live over SSE and accept interventions. There is no hosted backend any more — the old
# api.usedonald.com is gone. See "Self-hosting the live stack" in the root readme.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DONALD_API=https://your-own-api.example.com

# Optional. Enables /api/interpret (typed and spoken operator instructions) and prompt
# suggestions. Left unset in production on purpose: the routes are public and unmetered.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
